## Rule Details

This rule disallows duplicate test expressions in `case` clauses of `switch` statements.

Examples of **incorrect** code for this rule:

```
/*eslint no-duplicate-case: "error"*/
const a = 1,
 one = 1;
switch (a) {
 case 1:
 break;
 case 2:
 break;

 default:
 break;
}
switch (a) {
 case one:
 break;
 case 2:
 break;

 default:
 break;
}
switch (a) {
 case "1":
 break;
 case "2":
 break;

 default:
 break;
}
