Source: Rust Api Guidelines > Type safety > Builders enable construction of complex values (C-BUILDER) > Non-consuming builders (preferred) > The benefit

#### The benefit

By using borrows throughout, `Command` can be used conveniently for both
one-liner and more complex constructions:

```rust
// One-liners
Command::new("/bin/cat").arg("file.txt").spawn();

// Complex configuration
let mut cmd = Command::new("/bin/ls");
if size_sorted {
 cmd.arg("-S");
}
cmd.arg(".");
cmd.spawn();
```

