Source: Csharp Coding Conventions > Tools and analyzers > Language guidelines > Event handling

### Event handling

- Use a lambda expression to define an event handler that you don't need to remove later:

```
public Form2()
{
 this.Click += (s, e) =>
 {
 MessageBox.Show(
 ((MouseEventArgs)e).Location.ToString());
 };
}
```
The lambda expression shortens the following traditional definition.

```
public Form1()
{
 this.Click += new EventHandler(Form1_Click);
}
void Form1_Click(object? sender, EventArgs e)
{
 MessageBox.Show(((MouseEventArgs)e).Location.ToString());
}
```

